From fb9eef308d488a2f1a2e7be5b4f3bf140f484096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:29:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] bwfm: never hold up the boot; bounded bring-up of a chip
 left running by a warm reset

A warm reset does not power-cycle the chip: the old firmware may still be
running, or the chip may be asleep, and a boot hung for minutes right
after "chip 43430 rev 1".  Each failed SDIO command costs the sdiob
timeout (5 s, CMD53 with retries up to 20 s), the driver's register
loops ran up to thousands of them, and a failed backplane read returned
0, on which the EROM scan never terminates.

- all chip access (bring-up, firmware download, firmware init) runs in a
  task; attach waits for it at most hw.bwfm.attach_wait (10 s) and then
  lets the boot continue; a later completion is announced to devd as
  WIFI ATTACH (devd.conf runs pccard_ether bwfmN startchildren);
- bus errors are counted; after 8 in a row the card is declared dead,
  further accesses fail at once and the device stays idle;
- failed reads return all ones; clock waits are bounded by time, the
  EROM scan by entry count;
- before the backplane is touched: card interrupts off, F2 disabled,
  KSO written until the chip reports KSO and DEVON (bounded);
- firmware verification after download compares the first 4 KB by
  default (hw.bwfm.verify_fw=1: everything), halving the download time
  on the slow SDIO bus; a verification mismatch is now an error;
- the bring-up logs its phase times.
---
 sbin/devd/devd.conf         |   7 +
 sys/dev/bwfm/bwfm.c         |   4 +-
 sys/dev/bwfm/if_bwfm_sdio.c | 381 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 3 files changed, 294 insertions(+), 98 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sbin/devd/devd.conf b/sbin/devd/devd.conf
index 4ffb8cde4..c8109bd88 100644
--- a/sbin/devd/devd.conf
+++ b/sbin/devd/devd.conf
@@ -51,6 +51,13 @@ attach 0 {
 	device-name "$wifi-driver-regex";
 	action "/etc/pccard_ether $device-name startchildren";
 };
+# A WiFi driver whose firmware came up after attach returned (bwfm(4)
+# does not hold up the boot for a slow or stuck chip) reports it here.
+notify 0 {
+	match "system"		"WIFI";
+	match "type"		"ATTACH";
+	action "/etc/pccard_ether $subsystem startchildren";
+};
 detach 0 {
 	device-name "$wifi-driver-regex";
 	action "/etc/pccard_ether $device-name stopchildren";
